# C4 (use-case 05), conditional-branch form: a disjunction of closed
# shapes keyed on a data-supplied field VIA A REFERENCE silently passes
# vet; the same composition as one document is refused.
# expected: verdict: invalid, exit 1 (plan "free" selects the free branch,
#           which pins sso: false; data says sso: true -- one-document
#           evaluation reports [aontu/scalar_value] at $.t.e.plan, exit 1)
# actual: verdict: valid, exit 0 -- { plan: $.t.p } resolved against the
#         schema-side 'string' only, so the data's sso: true just picks
#         the pro branch and the plan tie is never enforced
# run: aontu vet stale-reference-branch.aon stale-reference-branch.json
Ent: type( close({ plan: "free", sso: false }) | close({ plan: "pro", sso: boolean }) )
t: { p: string, e: $.Ent & { plan: $.t.p } }
